This uses kprobes to trace the new_sync_read() and
new_sync_write() kernel functions. As kprobes is an
unstable interface, there's no guarantee that these will
work across different kernel versions, and we've already
encountered kernels where they are not available for
tracing (inlined). The BCC version employs the
workaround, by tracing higher-level __vfs_read() and
__vfs_write() internal functions and then filtering for
those that are synchronous.
