The address family number mappings (e.g., AF_INET
== 2) is specific to Linux, and is defined in the
include/linux/socket.h header (the table is included on
the following pages). Other kernels use their own
number mappings.
Since the traced calls occur at a relatively low rate
(compared to packet events), the overhead of this tool is
expected to be negligible.
The source to sofamily(8) is:
