The reported latency is for the connect() syscall only.
For some applications, including the ssh(1) processes
seen in the earlier output, this spans the network
latency to establish a connection to the remote host.
Other applications may create non-blocking sockets
(SOCK_NONBLOCK), and the connect() syscall may
return early before the connection is completed. This
can be seen in the example output as the final curl(1)
connection that results in an “In progress” result. To
measure the full connection latency for these non-
blocking calls requires instrumenting more events; an
example is the later soconnlat(8) tool.
