This tool records a starting timestamp in a @connstart
map during the entry to connect(2), keyed by the
process ID and file descriptor. If this connect(2) is a
failure (unless it is non-blocking and returned with
EINPROGRESS), or close(2) was issued, it deletes the
timestamp to stop tracking that connection. When the
first read or recv syscall is entered on the socket file
descriptor seen earlier, it tracks the file descriptor in
@readfd so that it can be fetched on syscall exit, and
finally the starting time read from the @connstart map.
This timespan is similar to the TCP time to first byte
described earlier, but with a small difference: the
connect(2) duration is included.
