DNS is a common source of production latency. At
Shopify, the bpftrace version of this tool was executed
on a Kubernetes cluster to characterize a DNS latency
issue in production. The data did not point to an issue
with a certain server or target of the lookup, but rather
latency when many lookups were in flight. The issue
was further debugged and found to be a cloud limit on
the number of UDP sessions that could be open on each
host. Increasing the limit resolved the issue.
