time can be calculated: in this case it was 0.1% (32 /
30416).
This works by tracing the stolen_clock paravirt ops call
using kprobes of the Xen and KVM versions:
xen_stolen_clock() and kvm_stolen_clock(). This is
called on many frequent events, such as context
switches and interrupts, so the overhead of this tool
may be noticeable depending on your workload.
The source to cpustolen(8) is:
